ue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in v4.7.stable.mono.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 17134) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.3141) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-7700 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 23.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (96000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe new `Scene Paint Mode` does not seem to work correctly if **any parent node** has scaling. (global scaling is not one)\n\nWhen the parent is scaled, the disabled \"allow overlapping\" feature stops working, and it paints several scenes over each other.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60881c79-75ce-40a7-900e-84d4efac04d4\n\n\n---\n\nThe Paint Mode snap also seems to be ignoring the **Grid Offset** setting.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6fb8a13-4a83-40e1-a971-95aab18bfc8f\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Broken overlap inside scaled snap\n- Create a node2d and scale it higher than 1.0\n- Select paint mode with the scaled node.\n- Paint a scene with snap turned on\n \nResult: Overlaps multiple scenes, ignoring overlay option\nExpected: Don't overlay if the overlap option is not turned on.\n\n2. Snap offset is ignored\n- Set the snap offset.\n- Select paint mode with snap\n\nResult: Uses correct snap, but ignores snap offset completely\nExpected: Snap offset is reflected in the Paint Mode snap\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[scene paint snap broken MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29292432/scene.paint.snap.broken.MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repi